          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.192,
            0.845,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "Binairo, also known as Takuzu, is a logic puzzle with simple rules. Binairo is generally played on a square grid with no particular size. Some cells start out filled with two symbols: here horizontal and vertical lines. The rest of the cells are empty. The task is to fill cells in such a way that:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.272,
            0.846,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "1. Each row and each column must contain an equal number of horizontal and vertical lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.32,
            0.77,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "2. More than two horizontal or vertical lines can’t be adjacent."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.35,
            0.614,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "3. Each row is unique. Each column is unique."
        },
        {
